Subject: [PATCH] cmd/storj-sim: wait for jobq to listen before its clients

satellite-repairer, satellite-core and satellite-rangedloop only waited
for the migration to exit, so storj-sim started them at the same time as
jobq. Under -race jobq can take longer than the repairer's first Select:
the dial to the jobq address is refused, repairer.go returns the error
from processWhileQueueHasItems, the process exits 1 and --failfast
cancels the whole network ("network canceled: satellite-repairer/0
failed: exit status 1", Jenkins test_stork_patched #233, Postgres
branch).

jobq has an Address, so its Started fence is only released once the
port accepts connections; wait on it.

Temporary: drop once upstream storj-sim orders these processes itself.
---
diff --git a/cmd/storj-sim/network.go b/cmd/storj-sim/network.go
index 475009241..b051d0399 100644
--- a/cmd/storj-sim/network.go
+++ b/cmd/storj-sim/network.go
@@ -571,6 +571,7 @@ func newNetwork(flags *Flags) (*Processes, error) {
 			coreProcess.ExecBefore["run"] = jobqArg
 		}
 		coreProcess.WaitForExited(migrationProcess)
+		coreProcess.WaitForStart(jobqProcess)
 
 		rangedLoopProcess := processes.New(Info{
 			Name:       fmt.Sprintf("satellite-rangedloop/%d", i),
@@ -584,6 +585,7 @@ func newNetwork(flags *Flags) (*Processes, error) {
 			rangedLoopProcess.ExecBefore["run"] = jobqArg
 		}
 		rangedLoopProcess.WaitForExited(migrationProcess)
+		rangedLoopProcess.WaitForStart(jobqProcess)
 
 		adminProcess := processes.New(Info{
 			Name:       fmt.Sprintf("satellite-admin/%d", i),
@@ -608,6 +610,8 @@ func newNetwork(flags *Flags) (*Processes, error) {
 			repairProcess.ExecBefore["run"] = jobqArg
 		}
 		repairProcess.WaitForExited(migrationProcess)
+		// jobq must be listening, the repairer exits on its first failed dial
+		repairProcess.WaitForStart(jobqProcess)
 
 		garbageCollectionProcess := processes.New(Info{
 			Name:       fmt.Sprintf("satellite-garbage-collection/%d", i),
